    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "JDG3:10",
        "textualBasisJa": "The LORD’s Spirit came on him, and he judged Israel; and he went out to war, and the LORD delivered Cushan Rishathaim king of Mesopotamia into his hand. His hand prevailed against Cushan Rishathaim."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG6:34",
        "textualBasisJa": "But the LORD’s Spirit came on Gideon, and he blew a trumpet; and Abiezer was gathered together to follow him."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG11:29",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then the LORD’s Spirit came on Jephthah, and he passed over Gilead and Manasseh, and passed over Mizpah of Gilead, and from Mizpah of Gilead he passed over to the children of Ammon."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG13:25",
        "textualBasisJa": "The LORD’s Spirit began to move him in Mahaneh Dan, between Zorah and Eshtaol."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG14:6",
        "textualBasisJa": "The LORD’s Spirit came mightily on him, and he tore him as he would have torn a young goat with his bare hands, but he didn’t tell his father or his mother what he had done."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG14:19",
        "textualBasisJa": "The LORD’s Spirit came mightily on him, and he went down to Ashkelon and struck thirty men of them. He took their plunder, then gave the changes of clothing to those who declared the riddle. His anger burned, and he went up to his father’s house."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG15:14",
        "textualBasisJa": "When he came to Lehi, the Philistines shouted as they met him. Then the LORD’s Spirit came mightily on him, and the ropes that were on his arms became as flax that was burned with fire; and his bands dropped from off his hands."
      }
    ],
